// Copy this file to `Local.xcconfig` (git-ignored) in the same directory and fill in real,
// public values for local development. Do not commit `Local.xcconfig`.
//
// OMEN_SUPABASE_URL and OMEN_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY are the public Supabase project URL and anon
// key (safe to ship in a client build — Supabase RLS enforces access control server-side).
// Never put a service-role key or any other secret here.
//
// URL SYNTAX — READ BEFORE PASTING A URL. In xcconfig, `//` begins a comment, so a bare
// `https://host` silently truncates to `https:`. The older `https:$()//host` workaround no
// longer works: Xcode 26 strips comments *before* expanding `$()`, so it also yields `https:`.
// Use `$(OMEN_SLASH)$(OMEN_SLASH)` as below — `OMEN_SLASH` is defined in `Base.xcconfig`,
// which includes this file. Verified on Xcode 26.6. The truncation is silent: a bad value
// reaches `Info.plist` and ships in the build without any warning. The anon key needs no
// escaping — only URLs do.
//
// To verify after editing, without printing secrets to the terminal:
//   xcodebuild -project mobile/ios/OmenIOS/OmenIOS.xcodeproj -scheme OmenIOS \
//     -showBuildSettings | grep OMEN_ | awk '{print $1, length($3)}'
// A length of 6 means the value truncated to `https:`.

OMEN_API_BASE_URL = https:$(OMEN_SLASH)$(OMEN_SLASH)your-local-or-staging-api.example.com
OMEN_SUPABASE_URL = https:$(OMEN_SLASH)$(OMEN_SLASH)your-project.supabase.co
OMEN_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = your-public-anon-key

// O6 crash reporting. Copy the DSN from the Sentry "iOS" project under the
// `valor-ventures-llc` org (Settings → Projects → iOS → Client Keys (DSN)).
// Blank disables the handler entirely — the same blank-is-off contract Android
// (`omen.androidSentryDsn`) and the backend (`SENTRY_DSN`) use.
// This file is git-ignored; the DSN never belongs in Base.xcconfig.
OMEN_IOS_SENTRY_DSN =
